# XBD <stdlib.h>
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Semantic content of the header page: values, relations and properties.
# The presence of each name and type comes with the Tier 0 generator.

assertion  XBD.stdlib.h.001
anchor     basedefs/stdlib.h.html#DESCRIPTION/EXIT_FAILURE
class      required
since      1988
says       EXIT_SUCCESS is an integer constant expression with value 0 and
           EXIT_FAILURE one with a value from 1 to 125.
note       The range 1 to 125 is the POSIX addition to ISO C.
test       t/001-exit-codes.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.stdlib.h.002
anchor     basedefs/stdlib.h.html#DESCRIPTION/RAND_MAX
class      required
since      1988
says       RAND_MAX is an integer constant expression of at least 32767.
test       t/002-rand-max.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.stdlib.h.003
anchor     basedefs/stdlib.h.html#DESCRIPTION/MB_CUR_MAX
class      required
since      1988
says       MB_CUR_MAX has type size_t and is positive, and is 1 in the POSIX
           locale (the default for a program that has not called setlocale(), and
           the one named by "C" or "POSIX").
test       t/003-mb-cur-max.c
nomutant   run-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.stdlib.h.004
anchor     basedefs/stdlib.h.html#DESCRIPTION/WNOHANG
class      required
since      2024
says       <stdlib.h> also defines WNOHANG and WUNTRACED; they are flag values
           for waitpid(), so each is nonzero and they share no bit.
note       The page points to <sys/wait.h>, where the options argument of
           waitpid() is an inclusive OR of flags; that a flag has a bit of its
           own is the reading of that.
test       t/004-wait-options.c
nomutant   compile-time check of header content; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
